"use strict";Object.defineProperty(exports,"__esModule",{value:!0}),exports.COMPACTION_PROMPT=exports.COMPACTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT=void 0,exports.COMPACTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT="You are a helpful AI assistant tasked with summarizing conversations for seamless continuation.\n\nWhen asked to summarize, provide a STRUCTURED summary using the exact format below.\nThe summary MUST preserve enough detail for the next agent turn to avoid redoing completed work.\nFocus on concrete file paths, type names, and step progress — not vague descriptions.\n\nYour summary should be comprehensive enough to continue the work without duplicating anything already done.",exports.COMPACTION_PROMPT='Summarize our conversation for continuation using this EXACT structure:\n\n## Completed Steps\nList which workflow steps (1-8) are fully completed. E.g.: "Steps 1-4 completed."\n\n## Files Already Written/Modified\nList EVERY file that was created or modified, with full path. E.g.:\n- CREATED: /path/to/HomeView.swift\n- MODIFIED: /path/to/ContentView.swift\n\n## Types/Classes Already Declared\nList EVERY struct, class, enum, protocol, interface, or component that was created or exists in merged files. E.g.:\n- struct HomeView (in HomeView.swift)\n- enum DesignTokens (in DesignTokens.swift)\n\n## Current Step In Progress\nWhat step/file was being worked on when interrupted.\n\n## Remaining Work\nList incoming code files that have NOT yet been merged.\n\n## Key Decisions\nUser preferences, conflict resolutions, and constraints that must persist.\n\nIMPORTANT: Be SPECIFIC with file paths and type names. The next turn will use this to avoid creating duplicate files or redeclaring existing types.';